# Default: normalize to LF in the repo AND in every checkout.
#
# `eol=lf` and not "check out native": Biome's formatter (and every gate built
# on it) expects LF, so a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true used to fail
# `npm run lint` on all 114 files before a single line had been edited. The
# two `#!/usr/bin/env node` scripts are also unusable from WSL with CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures are byte-exact samples of what real browsers and spreadsheets emit.
# EOL normalization would rewrite the CRLF records in the CSV exports, so a
# fresh clone would test a different file than the one that was committed.
# NOTE: last matching rule wins, so this block must stay BELOW the `*` line.
tests/fixtures/** -text
